## Indexed Job retry defaults

`spec.job_template.spec.backoff_limit_per_index` and `spec.job_template.spec.max_failed_indexes` have **provider defaults of `0`**, preserving provider `3.2.1` behavior for Indexed Job templates. These are not Kubernetes API defaults. These two fields are exceptions to the optional-field null normalization described in the migration guide.

Omitting or removing either argument selects `0`; it does not unset the corresponding Indexed Job template API field or select unlimited failures. Leaving an implicit `0` omitted, or removing an explicit `0`, does not change these retry settings.

- Changing a nonzero `backoff_limit_per_index` to its default `0`, including by removing the argument, requires replacement of the CronJob. The provider retains this replacement behavior even though Kubernetes supports updates to CronJob templates.
- Changing a nonzero `max_failed_indexes` to its default `0`, including by removing the argument, updates the CronJob in place.

